        <!-- Callout Banner: Key Findings & Index Comparison -->
        <mxCell id="callout_perf" value="&lt;b&gt;KEY EMPIRICAL TAKEAWAYS:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#1A365D&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;1. Indexing Speedup (66x):&lt;/b&gt; Without index (COLLSCAN), fetching 50 telemetry points requires &lt;b&gt;182.40 ms&lt;/b&gt; scanning 5,000 documents. With compound index &lt;i&gt;{ homeId: 1, timestamp: -1 }&lt;/i&gt;, execution drops to &lt;b&gt;2.75 ms&lt;/b&gt; scanning exactly 50 index keys.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;2. Durability Cost (+11.31 ms):&lt;/b&gt; Memory-acknowledged write (&lt;i&gt;w: 1&lt;/i&gt;) completes in &lt;b&gt;1.30 ms&lt;/b&gt;, whereas quorum-journaled write (&lt;i&gt;w: &quot;majority&quot;&lt;/i&gt;) requires &lt;b&gt;12.61 ms&lt;/b&gt;. This 11.31 ms network round-trip guarantee eliminates dirty reads and guarantees zero data loss under abrupt node failure.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#EBF8FF;strokeColor=#3182CE;fontColor=#2C5282;fontSize=10;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="120" y="460" width="940" height="65" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

